  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EA17 2010 - Cross Sectoral Emergency Response to LRA attacks in Western Equatoria State, Sudan.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The 12 month proposed programme will provide support to the Diocese of Tombura Yambio to deliver much needed food, non-food items, basic shelter, water and sanitation, and education and emergency health services for conflict affected households in 7 Counties of Western Equatoria State. The programme will also provide some support to strengthen the systems of the Diocese of Tombura Yambio to ensure more sustainable organisational capacity.

The proposed intervention will build on the existing emergency programme run by the Diocese which was supported through the CI Appeal EA30 2009. It will continue existing activities, and expand to new counties and sectors.

The overall goal of the intervention is &#x2018;to prevent excess mortality and morbidity among IDP, refugee and host communities whose lives have been directly affected by the campaign of terrorising attacks waged by the LRA rebel forces in Western Equatoria State, Sudan&#x2019;.  

The specific objective is: to meet the immediate and initial recovery needs of those displaced by LRA attacks in the most insecure and unassisted Counties of Western Equatoria through food, NFI and shelter assistance, education and access to and use of health, water and sanitation facilities.

Result One:	The nutritional and support needs of 18,000 identified at-risk individuals are met.

Result Two: 	5,000 newly displaced households have sufficient basic goods and supplies to meet personal hygiene needs, prepare and eat food, and build, maintain or repair shelters to ensure their dignity, safety and well-being.

Result Three: 	7500 people in Western Equatoria State have improved access to safe and sustainably managed water facilities.

Result Four:	Improved awareness on public heath and good hygiene practices within the targeted Payams and villages.

Result Five:	1500 Children displaced by conflict have increased access to basic primary education in the targeted Payams and villages 

Result Six: 	The Development and Peace Office has increased capacity to respond to emerging health needs in the target Payams and villages.
  
Result Seven:	The Development and Peace Office have strengthened systems to effectively manage existing and future humanitarian and development programmes within the Diocese of Tombura Yambio.</narrative>
  </description>
